adjudication.rationale:
In `apps/web/pages/api/webhook/app-credential.ts`, the webhook secret is validated via a normal string inequality check:

```ts
if (req.headers[... ] !== process.env.CALCOM_WEBHOOK_SECRET) {
  return res.status(403)
}
```

This is not a constant-time comparison. For secret validation, using standard `===/!==` can theoretically leak information via timing differences (best practice is `crypto.timingSafeEqual` on normalized `Buffer`s). So the diff does introduce the exact pattern the finding calls out.

The diff introduces `parseRefreshTokenResponse` which explicitly does:

```ts
if (!refreshTokenResponse.data.refresh_token) {
  refreshTokenResponse.data.refresh_token = "refresh_token";
}
```

So when a token refresh response (or the minimally validated response under credential sharing) lacks `refresh_token`, the code assigns the literal string "refresh_token" instead of preserving the prior refresh token or failing. This is a concrete behavior present in the diff and can result in an invalid refresh token being stored/propagated.
